  "scientific_interpretation": {
    "what_is_established": [
      "The current sixteen-query conjunctive gate is too sampling-sensitive to be a reliable sole selector across all three development domains.",
      "This conclusion is driven by TNG100 finite-population tail, Q4, and two-point comparisons, not by high-k power or residual-RMS instability.",
      "A simulation-domain-blind empirical residual law is strongly stressed whenever TNG100 is transferred to or from another domain; SIMBA and Swift are mutually much more compatible.",
      "The strict maximum-energy comparison behaves like a coin flip under exchangeable truth-oracle draws, while the already consumed V72 TNG100 candidate-versus-control disadvantage is statistically resolved."
